If the type is valuable you get the knowledge that specific type
is valuable and you have the rest of your big stack of them.
That plus the luck bonus that might or might not have any
effect depending on your previous luck number.  But you also
lose the ability to sell that gem to a shp keeper without
killing that unicorn to get that gem back.  While there are
times I'll specifically want to kill a co-aligned unicorn those
times aren't related to selling items to shop keepers.

If the unicorn is not interested in your junk, you have learned
more than the identification of one type of colored glass.  You
have learned that each and every other gem type of that color
is valuable.  That plus a well trained pet could drain a shop
keeper of this cash.  To a great extent, knowing conclusively
that a gem is valuable or not is as good as having it fully
identified.  If I read the shop code right you can get a tiny
amount of cash selling a "red gem called glass" gem but zero
for a "worthless piece of red glass".

